---
export const prerender = true

import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import aboutImage from '../images/about-image.png'
---

<Layout
  title="About - Christopher Harley"
  description="About Christopher Harley, Design Engineer"
>
  <section
    class="max-w-max-width mx-auto px-edge-padding pb-section-v-space flex flex-col gap-section-v-space mb-section-v-space mt-section-v-space"
  >
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-gutter items-start">
      <div class="md:col-span-5 relative w-full aspect-3/4 overflow-hidden">
        <Image
          src={aboutImage}
          alt="Christopher Harley Portrait"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover grayscale"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-7 flex flex-col pt-8 md:pt-0">
        <h1 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-text-primary mb-unit">
          Christopher Harley
        </h1>
        <div
          class="space-y-6 text-text-secondary font-body-lg text-body-lg max-w-prose mb-12"
        >
          <p>
            My path to frontend development wasn’t exactly a straight line. It
            began with a decade in the U.S. Army, where I learned to lead, plan
            under pressure, and turn complicated objectives into clear,
            executable systems. From there, it moved through Berklee College of
            Music, UX design, and software engineering—an unusual combination
            that continues to shape how I approach every project. Today, I’m a
            design-minded frontend developer with more than eight years of
            experience creating thoughtful, high-performance digital
            experiences. I’ve built product features inside a Fortune 500
            fintech environment, managed updates across hundreds of
            client-facing interfaces, and taken independent projects from
            initial concept through design, development, testing, and
            deployment.
          </p>
          <p>
            I’m most at home where design and engineering overlap: translating
            strong visual concepts into responsive, accessible code without
            losing the details that made the designs compelling. Away from the
            screen, I’m a drummer, electronic music producer, and DJ. Whether
            I’m arranging a track or building an interface, I’m usually chasing
            the same thing: something technically precise, creatively
            distinctive, and effortless for the person experiencing it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6 items-start sm:items-center mt-auto border-t border-border-muted/30 pt-8"
        >
          <a
            href="/christopher_harley_resume.pdf"
            download
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 border border-outline bg-transparent hover:bg-surface-container-low hover:border-text-primary transition-colors duration-200 text-text-primary"
          >
            <span class="font-label-mono text-label-mono mr-2"
              >Download Resume (PDF)</span
            >
            <span
              class="material-symbols-outlined"
              style="font-variation-settings: 'FILL' 0;">download</span
            >
          </a>
          <a
            href="/contact"
            class="font-label-mono text-label-mono text-text-primary hover:text-primary transition-colors duration-200 flex items-center gap-2"
          >
            Get in touch
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-body-md"
              >arrow_forward</span
            >
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
